 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items?limit=<1..100>&cursor=<cursor>` →
+  `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": "..."}`: items ordered by `id`.
+  `limit` defaults to 20. Pass `next_cursor` unchanged as `cursor` to fetch
+  the next page; the final page has `next_cursor: null`. Invalid limits and
+  cursors return HTTP-shaped status 400 with `{"error": "..."}`.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
